Z||000000||PeaceDawg||05-26-2001||07:27 PM||||I have a '85 v6 that won't start. Constantly floods..all 6 spark plugs are soaked in gas.<BR>Any ideas on why this is happening and what I might be able to do to get my car running again?  I take the plugs out...dry them and try to restart...it almost starts and then they are flooded again.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||PBJ||05-26-2001||07:36 PM||||Would suggest scan ecm with engine cold, will probably find ecm coolant temp sensor reads -35 all of the time.  This is a differant sensor than the dash guage.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||05-27-2001||07:35 AM||||A fella contacted me once with the exact same problem- we tried the sensor thing -no go. Finally he just bought new plugs and the beast fired right up. ||||reg||1
