Z||000012||PeaceDawg||06-04-2001||08:04 PM||||Put in a new coolant temperature sensor. The car fired up no problems. 3rd time that it was started service engine soon light came on.  Shut the car off and read the codes and it is saying that the problem is the coolant temperature sensor, which was just replaced and is new.  Not even 5 minutes with the new sensor.  So the car is flooding out again and won't start.  All of the plugs are equally soaked with gas.  I don't think that the problem is with the sensor as it is new, But for some reason the ecm is getting the idea that there is something wrong with the temperature sensor.  Any ideas?? Help!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
